{"review":"approved","flags":[{"page":22,"note":"The second log line writes '… · log(θ/3)³' with a multiplication sign; it should be '+ log(θ/3)³' (the next line is correct)."},{"page":58,"note":"The values labelled σ² (1.15, 17.08) are sample standard deviations; the variances are 1.33 and 291.67. P(60 | Yes) is printed as 0.15 × 10⁻⁹⁵; with mean 84.33 and SD 1.15 we get about 1.3 × 10⁻⁹⁷. The decision (No) is unaffected."},{"page":60,"note":"P(3.5 | Pass) = 0.1056 could not be reproduced: with the Pass hours (4.5, 7, 8, 9) the Gaussian density at 3.5 is 0.0355 (sample SD) or 0.0228 (population SD). The answer (Fail) is the same."},{"page":65,"note":"The side calculation '(3 + 14/5 + 28) = 0.00002396' appears to be a leftover; the correct Not-sports score is 0.00000572 (slide p.66)."}],"recall":{"defs":[["Likelihood","Probability of the data as a function of θ."],["Prior","Belief about θ before seeing data."],["Posterior","Belief about θ after seeing data."],["MAP estimate","θ maximising the posterior."],["Naïve Bayes","Classifier assuming conditional independence of features given the class."],["Laplace smoothing","Add-one pseudo-counts to avoid zero probabilities."]],"formulas":["\\theta_{MLE}=\\arg\\max_\\theta\\sum_i\\log f(X_i|\\theta)","\\theta_{MAP}=\\arg\\max_\\theta P(D|\\theta)P(\\theta)","v_{OB}=\\arg\\max_{v}\\sum_{h}P(v|h)P(h|D)","\\hat Y=\\arg\\max_kP(Y=y_k)\\prod_iP(X_i|Y=y_k)","P(A_i|C)=\\frac{N_{ic}+1}{N_c+d}"],"takeaways":["MLE: maximise the log-likelihood of IID data.","Gaussian noise → least squares; Bernoulli → log-loss; Laplace → MAE.","MAP adds a prior; equals MLE with a flat prior.","Bayes optimal averages hypotheses; Gibbs samples one (≤ 2× error).","Naïve Bayes multiplies per-feature likelihoods; smooth counts; Gaussian for numbers; bag of words for text."],"confused":[["MLE vs MAP","Likelihood only vs likelihood × prior."],["MAP hypothesis vs Bayes optimal","Single best h vs posterior-weighted vote."],["Density vs probability","Gaussian NB uses densities."],["Multinomial vs Bernoulli NB","Counts vs presence/absence."]],"minute":"Bayesian learning estimates parameters with probability. MLE maximises the log-likelihood of IID data: under Gaussian noise it gives least squares, for Bernoulli labels the logistic log-loss with gradient (y − σ)x, under Laplace noise the absolute error. MAP multiplies by a prior and equals MLE when the prior is flat. For prediction, the Bayes optimal classifier weights every hypothesis by its posterior, and Gibbs samples one at no more than twice the error. Naïve Bayes assumes features are independent given the class and predicts argmax P(y)ΠP(xᵢ|y): counts with Laplace smoothing for categories, Gaussians for numbers, word counts for text."},"flashcards":[["Distribution","Model + parameter θ",5],["IID","Independent, identically distributed samples",7],["Bayes' theorem","$P(\\theta|D)=\\frac{P(D|\\theta)P(\\theta)}{P(D)}$",8],["MLE recipe","Write LL(θ), differentiate, solve",9],["Gaussian noise MLE","Least squares",14],["Logistic LL gradient","$\\sum(y-\\sigma(\\theta^Tx))x_j$",16],["Laplace noise MLE","Mean absolute error",24],["MAP","$\\arg\\max P(D|h)P(h)$",25],["Bayes optimal","$\\arg\\max_v\\sum_hP(v|h)P(h|D)$",31],["Gibbs bound","$E[err_{Gibbs}]\\le2E[err_{BO}]$",33],["NB assumption","$P(X_1..X_n|Y)=\\prod P(X_j|Y)$",41],["NB rule","$\\arg\\max_kP(y_k)\\prod_iP(X_i|y_k)$",42],["Laplace smoothing","$\\frac{N_{ic}+1}{N_c+d}$",50],["m-estimate","$\\frac{N_{ic}+mp}{N_c+m}$",50],["NB variants","Bernoulli (binary), multinomial (counts), Gaussian (real)",70]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what","h1"],"deep":["b-param"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["b-mlml"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["b-bayes"],"viz":["bayesUpdate"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["b-mlerecipe"],"viz":["mleCurve"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["b-mlelin"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["b-mlelog"],"